  ],
  "mach:judgement": "Caution",
  "mach:judgementReason": "A current (June 2026) and technically strong neuroimaging foundation model — the V-JEPA 2 latent-predictive objective extended to 3D with a sparse Mixture-of-Experts backbone, pretrained on ~1.55M real clinical brain MRI scans and evaluated across 47 tasks with consistent gains over prior foundation models and CNN baselines. The training/evaluation code is openly MIT-licensed, which is a genuine plus. It is marked Caution rather than Assess because of the model weights: they are gated (institutional email and approval required, no redistribution) and licensed CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0 — both NonCommercial and NoDerivatives, which is not an open licence by the Open Source Definition or open-data norms. NoDerivatives in particular forbids fine-tuning and adaptation, the primary use case for a foundation model, and commercial use, monetization, and redistribution are all prohibited. The pretraining corpus is private PHI and unreleased, so results cannot be independently reproduced from the data. Evidence is currently the authors' own arXiv preprint (not yet peer-reviewed), and under the EU AI Act risk cap clinical neuroimaging diagnosis/prognosis is high-risk-candidate territory. Useful as a research starting point for academic teams who can accept the gated, non-commercial, no-derivatives terms; teams needing to fine-tune, deploy commercially, or redistribute should treat the weights as unusable and consider the openly licensed code instead. The MIT-licensed code is cataloged separately as neuro-jepa (software).",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-06-19",
  "schema:comment": "Weights are gated on HuggingFace (approval required) and licensed CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0; NoDerivatives forbids fine-tuning. Re-verify licence and gating on next review. Pretraining data is private NYU Langone PHI and not released.",
